# MQ05 "The Path of Dawn", first half: to Baurus's lead on the Mythic Dawn. MQ04 100 set MQ05 10. Jauffre sends the
# player to Baurus at Luther Broad's Boarding House (20); Baurus has the player tail the man watching him (25); the
# agent Astav Wirich follows Baurus to the cellar (30) and attacks (31); with him dead (32) Baurus has the body
# searched (34), the first "Commentaries" turns up (35), and Baurus names Tar-Meena at the Arcane University (36).
# The books, the Sponsor and Dagon Shrine (40 .. 100) are not drafted yet.
# DRAFT from tools/live/quest_brief.py (2026-11-12): not run yet.

# Jauffre at Cloud Ruler Temple first offers a place in the Blades (run 24b: "Yes, I will join the Blades." / "No,
# not right now." / "What are my duties as a Blade?"); the player joins (INFO 00037CED / 00037CEE: Blades rank 0
# and an Akaviri longsword). "Amulet of Kings" (INFO 0001EFE3) then sets 20, which moves Baurus to Luther Broad's.
case mq05_jauffre
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 10
run
player.moveto JauffreRef
wait 120
approach JauffreRef
talk JauffreRef
ask "Yes, I will join the Blades."
until 300 player.GetFactionRank Blades >= 0
ask "Amulet of Kings"
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 20
bye if open
end

# Baurus sits in Luther Broad's (MQ05BaurusLutherBroadsMarker). His greeting "Listen. I'm going to get up in a
# minute ..." (INFO 00022B13, MQ05 < 30) offers "The enemy has the Amulet.", "I found Uriel's heir." and "I'm ready
# when you are." (INFO 00022B16), which sets 25. The travel to the Imperial City is the player's: moveto stands in.
# To a standing player he only says "Sit down. Don't say anything. Just do what I say." (INFO 00022B11, a goodbye,
# player.GetSitting == 0; run 24c): the player takes the stool beside his (REFR 000549E1, 92 from MQ05BaurusChair).
case mq05_baurus_luther
run
player.moveto MQ05BaurusLutherBroadsMarker
wait 120
activate 000549E1
until 600 player.GetSitting >= 3
talk BaurusRef
ask "I'm ready when you are."
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 25
bye if open
end

# Baurus walks out to the cellar; Astav Wirich gets up and follows him (30, MQ05AstavWirichScript) and attacks
# (31). The player follows and fights beside Baurus (`defend BaurusRef`); Astav's death sets 32.
# This boundary saves while Baurus walks to the cellar door, as a player's save can: keep it (run 58a).
case mq05_astav
defend BaurusRef
until 3600 GetStage MQ05 >= 30
# Baurus first walks down to MQ05BaurusWaitMarker in the cellar; MQ05BaurusHeadForAmbush then needs the player in
# his cell (GetInSameCell player). Run 38b: a moveto at 30 left the player upstairs as he went down.
until 3600 BaurusRef.GetDistance MQ05BaurusWaitMarker < 100
run
player.moveto BaurusRef
until 3600 GetStage MQ05 >= 31
until 1800 GetStage MQ05 >= 32
expect MQ05AstavWirichRef.GetDead
end

# Baurus's greeting at 32 ("Search his body. I'll keep an eye out ...", INFO 00022B1A) sets 34. The first book is on
# Astav's body (QSTxMQ05CommentariesV1Script sets 35 when it leaves him); RemoveAllItems stands in for looting.
# Then Baurus's greeting ("Good work. ...", INFO 00022B1D) offers "What have you learned?" (INFO 00022B1E; run 24e),
# which offers: "The enemy has the Amulet." (MQ05.toldAmulet 2), "I found Uriel's heir." (toldMartin 2), and "What's
# our next move?" (INFO 00022B23, needs both), which sets 36.
case mq05_baurus_book
approach BaurusRef
activate BaurusRef
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 34
bye if open
run
MQ05AstavWirichRef.RemoveAllItems player
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 35
approach BaurusRef
talk BaurusRef
ask "What have you learned?"
ask "The enemy has the Amulet."
until 300 MQ05.toldAmulet == 2
ask "I found Uriel's heir."
until 300 MQ05.toldMartin == 2
ask "What's our next move?"
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 36
bye if open
end

# Tar-Meena at the Arcane University. "Mythic Dawn" (INFO 00024E7F) offers "I found one of their books." (INFO
# 00022B41), which offers "I need to find the Mythic Dawn." (INFO 00022B42), which offers "Where can I find these
# books?" (INFO 00022B43): Volume 2 and stage 40.
case mq05_tar_meena
run
player.moveto TarMeenaRef
wait 120
approach TarMeenaRef
talk TarMeenaRef
ask "Mythic Dawn"
ask "I found one of their books."
ask "I need to find the Mythic Dawn."
ask "Where can I find these books?"
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 40
expect player.GetItemCount MQ05CommentariesV2 >= 1
bye if open
end

# Phintias at First Edition. "Mysterium Xarxes" (INFO 00022B3C) offers "I need volumes 3 and 4." (50: Volume 3 is
# held for Gwinas, who is moved to MQ05GwinasStartMarker and walks to the shop); "Gwinas" (INFO 00022B46) sets 60.
# He only speaks of it in his shop (GetInCell ICMarketDistrictFirstEdition; run 24f met him elsewhere at 1 am: only
# "What have you got for sale?" and "Rumors"), so the player comes in shop hours.
case mq05_phintias
run
set gamehour to 10
until 7200 PhintiasRef.GetInCell ICMarketDistrictFirstEdition == 1
run
player.moveto PhintiasRef
wait 120
expect PhintiasRef.GetInCell ICMarketDistrictFirstEdition == 1
approach PhintiasRef
talk PhintiasRef
ask "Mysterium Xarxes"
ask "I need volumes 3 and 4."
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 50
ask "Gwinas"
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 60
bye if open
end

# Gwinas comes for his book; the player talks him out of it. "Commentaries, Volume Three" (INFO 00022B4C, MQ05 <
# 72) offers "Tell me about the Mythic Dawn cult." -> "Don't play stupid." -> "They killed the Emperor, you fool!"
# (INFO 0009532B) -> "You'd better give me that book." (INFO 0009532D: Volume 3 and stage 45) -> "I need the fourth
# book as well." (INFO 0009532E: 70, whose result hands over the Sponsor's note and sets 72).
case mq05_gwinas
run
player.moveto GwinasRef
wait 120
approach GwinasRef
talk GwinasRef
ask "Commentaries, Volume Three"
ask "Tell me about the Mythic Dawn cult."
ask "Don't play stupid."
ask "They killed the Emperor, you fool!"
ask "You'd better give me that book."
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 45
ask "I need the fourth book as well."
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 70
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 72
expect player.GetItemCount MQ05CommentariesV3 >= 1
bye if open
end

# 72 moves Baurus to MQ05BaurusStage72. "Mythic Dawn meeting" (INFO 00022CF0, 70 <= MQ05 < 75) sets 75: he leads
# the way to the Sunken Sewer.
case mq05_baurus_meeting
run
player.moveto BaurusRef
wait 120
approach BaurusRef
talk BaurusRef
ask "Mythic Dawn meeting"
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 75
bye if open
end

# Baurus reaches the sewer's lower hall (76, BaurusScript OnPackageDone; the Sponsor, RavenRef, is enabled). His
# greeting at 76 (INFO 00022CEB / 00022CEC) plans the meeting: "Alright. I'll cover you." (INFO 00022CF3) sets 78
# (Baurus meets the Sponsor, the player is the backup) and offers "I'm ready when you are."; MQ05Script then sets
# 79 once Baurus (MQ05.pointRef) sits at the table and the player is in ImperialSewersElvenGardens02: the player
# takes the backup's place above the room (MQ05BaurusBackupMoveMarker; run 25d stayed in the hall: 78 for good).
# Baurus leads (an escort: he walks on only while the player is close behind), so the player follows him
# (`follow`) and arrives after him at each loading door's far side, where a player coming through it stands: the
# Elven Gardens sewer (01, door 00023D2E: the gate wheel, the tunnel gate), the Sewer Waterworks (03, door 0006B0F7)
# and 01 again for the lower hall (door 0006AE80). (Run 44b: an `approach` teleport onto him in 01's cramped arrival
# room pushed him through the wall; 44d: the street door was never loaded once the player was already inside.)
# Out of the inn the player takes its street door (0002C210) after him, as a player does: an `approach` put the
# player 80 IN FRONT of him, in the sewer doorway, and he never went through it (55a; 44a the same).
case mq05_sewer_plan
defend BaurusRef
follow BaurusRef
until 1800 BaurusRef.GetInSameCell player == 0
activate 0002C210
wait 60
until 3600 BaurusRef.GetInCell ImperialSewersElvenGardens01 == 1
run
player.moveto 00023D2E
wait 60
until 3600 BaurusRef.GetInCell ImperialSewersElvenGardens03 == 1 || GetStage MQ05 >= 76
run
player.moveto 0006B0F7
wait 60
until 3600 BaurusRef.GetInCell ImperialSewersElvenGardens01 == 1
run
player.moveto 0006AE80
wait 60
until 3600 GetStage MQ05 >= 76
# The lower hall's creatures attack as the party arrives (60a, 16:38:17: four killed by `defend` while the
# talk opened, which closed it); a player deals with them first.
wait 90
approach BaurusRef
talk BaurusRef
ask "Alright. I'll cover you."
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 78
ask "I'm ready when you are."
# His answer ("Listen. I may not survive this ...", 000A31BF) offers three replies, each answered by a goodbye
# line; since the force greet's exit hold (af21975f) Goodbye stays hidden until one is picked, as in Oblivion.
ask "I understand. We'll do it - together."
bye if open
# He walks to the table in 02 only while his cell is loaded (54c replay: the player sent ahead to 02 left him
# standing in 01 for 9000 ticks; loading his cell moved him on), so the player stays with him until he is in 02.
until 3600 BaurusRef.GetInCell ImperialSewersElvenGardens02 == 1
follow
run
player.moveto MQ05BaurusBackupMoveMarker
wait 120
expect player.GetInCell ImperialSewersElvenGardens02 == 1
# MQ05Script sets 79 once Baurus sits at the table (run 38g: he sat, the meeting ran and he stood to fight before a
# sitting check was polled, so the case waits for the stage).
until 9000 GetStage MQ05 >= 79
end

# The Sponsor comes to the table room (80), the meeting goes wrong (81 or 82, both set 85) and the cultists
# attack; the player fights beside Baurus. The fourth book is on the Sponsor's body: taking it sets 90
# (MQ05CommentariesV4Script OnAdd). RemoveAllItems stands in for looting.
case mq05_sponsor
defend BaurusRef
until 3600 GetStage MQ05 >= 80
until 3600 GetStage MQ05 >= 85
until 1800 RavenRef.GetDead
run
RavenRef.RemoveAllItems player
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 90
end

# Tar-Meena reads the four books over three days: "Mythic Dawn" gives one hint a day (INFO 00024E6C -> 91, INFO
# 00024E6B -> 92, each needing MQ05.hintDay < GameDaysPassed), and on the third day (INFO 00022B3F) offers "Yes, I
# have them right here." (INFO 00024E81). Midnight is passed by setting the hour, as a player waits. Then: "Green Emperor Way Where Tower Touches Midday Sun" (93). The tomb of Prince Camarril (MQ05TombRef,
# Green Emperor Way) shows the map between 11.8 and 12.5 o'clock; activating it then sets 95 -> 100, which ends
# MQ05 and sets MQ06 10. `set gamehour` stands in for waiting until noon.
case mq05_shrine_clue
run
player.moveto TarMeenaRef
wait 120
approach TarMeenaRef
talk TarMeenaRef
ask "Mythic Dawn"
until 300 GetStageDone MQ05 91 == 1
bye if open
run
set gamehour to 23.9
wait 300
run
set gamehour to 10
player.moveto TarMeenaRef
wait 120
approach TarMeenaRef
talk TarMeenaRef
ask "Mythic Dawn"
until 300 GetStageDone MQ05 92 == 1
bye if open
run
set gamehour to 23.9
wait 300
run
set gamehour to 10
player.moveto TarMeenaRef
wait 120
approach TarMeenaRef
talk TarMeenaRef
ask "Mythic Dawn"
ask "Yes, I have them right here."
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 93
bye if open
run
player.moveto MQ05TombRef
wait 120
run
set gamehour to 12
wait 60
activate MQ05TombRef
until 300 GetStageDone MQ05 100
until 300 GetStage MQ06 >= 10
end
